31. API CONTRACT
Conceptual operations:
GET /identity/me
Returns the current identity representation.
GET /identity/me/continuity
Returns authorized continuity information.
PATCH /identity/me/handle
Changes the current @iriel handle.
POST /identity/me/separation
Explicitly separates identity only after appropriate
authorization.
GET /identity/me/history
Requires identity.history:read.
DELETE /identity/me/history
Executes applicable privacy and retention policy.
External providers must never receive identity history
through these APIs unless explicitly authorized and
required.
32. INTERACTION CONTRACT
The Interaction Layer must operate on:
current_identity
rather than:
historical_identity
The default interaction context should conceptually be:
current_identity
+
relevant_context
+
authorized_memory
and not:
current_identity
+
entire_identity_history
33. HUMAN PRINCIPLE
The person is allowed to evolve without becoming a
stranger to their own intelligence environment.
The ecosystem must adapt to the person.
The person must not be forced to repeatedly explain who
they are.
A person can change their name.
A person can change their @iriel handle.
A person can change devices.
A person can change platforms.
A person can change providers.
The iRiel should preserve the continuity that matters while
respecting the identity that exists now.
34. CORE PHILOSOPHY
The iRiel does not erase the past.
The iRiel does not force the past into the present.
The iRiel understands the difference.
Memory preserves what happened.
Context understands what changed.
Privacy controls what may be exposed.
Interaction respects who the person is now.
Resonance preserves continuity through change.
35. FINAL CANONICAL RULE
Remember continuity.
Understand change.
Learn from evolution.
Present the current identity.
Respect the person.